# The K-quant kernel's tiled variant reads its activation block 32 rows at a time on Xe2, takes
# 16 subgroups per work-group there, and gives Q5_K a 128-row tile

# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of
# patches/0003-0029. arcint 0.4.3 (DESIGN.md section 7.0.2bp).
#
# What changes:
#   fully_connected_gpu_kquant.cl   Under KQ_2D, the A operand of a sub-block is read by
#                       intel_sub_group_2d_block_read_16b_32r16x1c -- 32 rows in one message
#                       whose destination holds the rows in order, so rows 8u..8u+7 are row
#                       group u's operand unchanged (KQ_A_TALL 32: four row groups per read
#                       instead of one; the reads per super-block per subgroup 128 -> 32 on a
#                       64-row tile). Q5_K keeps the 8-row read (KQ_A_TALL 8) on its 128-row
#                       tile. The weight reads, the decodes and the matrix-unit calls are 0029's.
#   fully_connected_kernel_kquant.cpp   KQ_A_TALL from the type and the path (32 on the 2D path
#                       for Q4_K and the 224-byte Q6_K, 8 otherwise); the tiled kernel's
#                       work-group is 16 subgroups on Xe2 (kColumnGroupsXe2) and stays 8 on
#                       Xe-HPG's staged path; the row tile is per type: 128 for Q5_K where the
#                       2D loads run (a 64 KB staged tile otherwise, never taken), 64 for the
#                       rest on Xe2, 32 on Xe-HPG; the work-group of 16 only where the 2D
#                       loads run (Xe2's staged types -- the file-layout Q6_K, Q8_0 -- keep 8,
#                       unmeasured at 16); large_grf carries its measurement per architecture
#                       in its comment.
#   fully_connected_gpu_test.cpp   A 141-row Q5_K case (two tiles at 128 rows, the second
#                       partial); the small Q6_K shape 1,024 x 5,120 at 856 rows in the timing
#                       test (the served step's 47 launches of it were not timed before).
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-07 (UTC; the record's dates are local) -- correctness 22/22 on both cards, and
# 22/22 on every knob of the sweep --
# the timing test in device memory, warm, us per launch, 0029 -> 0030, the 24 GB card:
#   gate Q4_K 17,408 x 5,120 at M = 856 / 2,048: 3,373 / 7,178 -> 2,859 / 6,158 (-15 % / -14 %);
#   Q5_K 5,120^2: 1,044 / 2,215 -> 969 / 1,864 by the 128-row tile alone (-7 % / -16 %), 987 /
#   1,891 in the shipped build (8-row reads, 16 subgroups); the 224-byte Q6_K down projection 5,120 x 17,408: 4,400 /
#   9,973 -> 3,585 / 8,216 (-18 % / -18 %); the small Q6_K 1,024 x 5,120 at 856: 295 -> 244
#   (-17 %). The shipped build re-timed (m41): gate
#   2,859 / 6,163, Q5_K 987 / 1,891, Q6_K 3,590 / 8,229, the small Q6_K 250; the file-layout
#   Q6_K (type 14, the staged path on Xe2 at 8 subgroups) 9,918 at 856, as before. The 16 GiB card (Xe-HPG, staged path, 32 x 256, 8 subgroups): unchanged by
#   construction, its figures re-taken in the same window. M = 1 (the decode kernel) unchanged
#   on every shape: no knob leaked into kernel 0.
# The sweep (DESIGN 7.0.2bp): the 32-row read is the lever (-14 % gate, -16 % Q6_K at 8
#   subgroups); 16-row reads win less and lose 54 % on Q5_K; a work-group of 16 takes Q6_K
#   another 4 % and 4 loses; a prefetch of the next super-block's weight rows
#   (intel_sub_group_2d_block_prefetch_32b_16r8x1c; the transposed prefetch name does not
#   compile on bmg) loses on every type before the tall read (Q5_K 2.4x) and after it gains
#   2-3 % on the gate while costing Q5_K 4 % -- not shipped; the next sub-block's activation
#   prefetch (prefetch_16b_32r16x1c) loses everywhere; splitting the two matrix-unit calls
#   over the row groups is inert under the tall read and 1.9x slower on Q5_K without it.
#   The record's "Q5_K's six weight messages could be five" was a miscount: 44 dwords in
#   8-dword messages is six.
# Served on the 24 GB card (arcint 0.4.2, mixed form, u8 KV, +p11 base): the warm 856-token prefill 940 -> 1,001 t/s
# (first request 903 -> 962), 71,727 tokens 451 -> 464; the decode steps unchanged (54.8 / 73.7
# ms); Pruefstand 10/10; greedy outputs byte-identical at both depths (23e06c37e0d6,
# 086d5e71ad47); the 16 GiB card's staged-path figures unchanged (8.01 / 2.73 / 12.92 ms).
